  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and clients pay for demonstrated skill. They judge you by work samples and references, not by test labels.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is separating a hint from a verdict.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and aptitude and psychometric tests in career choice: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can explain results, suggest tasks to test hints and help you reflect. They can also repeat generic labels.
  </p>
  <p>
    Evidence from real tasks, honest reflection and judgment hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to plan tests of each hint; later, own the decision and the evidence.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general aptitude and psychometric tests in career choice path</h2>

